# More-Info Dialog & Domain State Controls

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

When someone selects a light, a thermostat, a lock or most other entities, Home Assistant opens the more-info dialog. It shows the entity’s state, the control that suits its kind of device, and, for people allowed to see them, its history, settings and related items.

A dashboard author cannot write this dialog or restyle it from a card. A theme can set its surface, corners, dividers and text colours. This page describes what the dialog contains so that you can write dashboards that open it, theme it and test it. The rules for dialogs in general, including confirmations, are owned by [Dialog / Modal](dialogs.html).

This page covers:

- More-Info Dialog & Domain State Controls
  - `ha-more-info-dialog`
    - `ha-more-info-info`
    - `ha-more-info-history`
    - `ha-more-info-logbook`
    - `ha-more-info-settings`
    - `ha-related-items`
    - `ha-state-control-light-brightness`
    - `ha-state-control-climate-temperature`
    - `ha-state-control-cover-position`
    - `ha-state-control-fan-speed`
    - `ha-state-control-humidifier-humidity`
    - `ha-state-control-lock-toggle`
    - `ha-state-control-toggle`
    - `ha-state-control-valve-position`
    - `ha-state-control-water_heater-temperature`
    - `ha-vacuum-state`
    - `ha-water_heater-state`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

The dialog has a header and a scrolling content area.

- The header has a close button, or a back button inside a sub-view, the entity name with its area and device above it, and buttons for history and settings. Administrators also get a three-dots menu.
- The content area shows the view: the state and control first, then history and logbook for most kinds of device.
- On a screen narrower than 870 pixels or shorter than 500 pixels the dialog opens as a bottom sheet instead, described on [Action Bar / Bottom Sheet](action-bar-bottom-sheet.html).

